      "body": "## Motivation\n\nOur self-hosted Ascend CI runners access public package sources through a cluster-level squid caching proxy. The old internal `nginx-pypi-cache` mirror (`cache-service.nginx-pypi-cache.svc.cluster.local`) is being retired, so this PR removes its references from the NPU CI workflow.\n\n## Changes (`citest_npu.yaml`, -8 / +1)\n\n- Drop `UV_INDEX_URL` / `UV_INSECURE_HOST` / `PIP_INDEX_URL` / `PIP_TRUSTED_HOST`; the public Huawei Cloud Ascend index (`UV_EXTRA_INDEX_URL`) and the remaining uv settings stay\n- Remove the APT source rewriting (`cache-service :8081`) and the two `pip config set` lines; the step is renamed from \"Config mirrors\" to \"Install uv\"\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `grep -r \"cache-service\\|nginx-pypi-cache\"` over the repo returns nothing\n- The workflow parses as valid YAML\n\nSigned-off-by: chenqi49 <479148871@qq.com>\n",
